{"from": "passage:lk-02-04", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-02-01", "note": "Luke tells the journey to Bethlehem for the census; Matthew 2:1 has the family already in Bethlehem when the Magi arrive."}
{"from": "passage:lk-02-06", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-02-01", "note": "The birth in Bethlehem: Matthew dates it to the days of Herod the king; Luke 2 names no Herod."}
{"from": "passage:lk-02-07", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-02-01", "note": "Luke's birth setting is a feeding trough because of no room in the kataluma; Matthew 2:11 finds the child in a house with the Magi."}
{"from": "passage:lk-02-39", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-02-23", "note": "Both record the family settling in Nazareth; Matthew's route is Egypt back to Judea then Nazareth after Herod's death, Luke's is direct after the presentation (2:39)."}
{"from": "claim:lk-02-02-enrollment-timing", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-02-01-herod-king", "note": "Matthew dates the birth to the days of Herod the king; Luke 2:2 ties the enrollment (and so the birth) to Quirinius, whose census Josephus places in 6 CE, about a decade after Herod's death. A difference between Gospels is never complicates."}
{"from": "claim:lk-02-39-return-nazareth", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-02-23-settled-nazareth", "note": "Luke has the family return to Nazareth directly after the presentation (2:39); Matthew has them settle in Nazareth only after the flight to Egypt, fearing Archelaus (Matt 2:22-23)."}
{"from": "claim:lk-02-21-circumcision-eighth-day", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:genesis-17-12", "note": "Cross-reference: Genesis 17:12 commands circumcision at eight days old. A biblical text is not independent evidence."}
{"from": "claim:lk-02-22-24-purification-turtledoves", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:leviticus-12-6-8", "note": "Cross-reference: Leviticus 12:6-8 sets the purification offering, and 12:8 the poor's two turtledoves or two young pigeons in place of a lamb. A biblical text is not independent evidence."}
{"from": "claim:lk-02-22-24-purification-turtledoves", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:exodus-13-2", "note": "Cross-reference: Exodus 13:2, 'Sanctify to me all the firstborn, whatever opens the womb', quoted in Luke 2:23. A biblical text is not independent evidence."}
